WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.887
NumPy provides common descriptive statistics directly on arrays.

00:00:04.887 --> 00:00:13.301
We can calculate the mean, median, minimum, maximum, standard deviation, and total sum with simple functions.

00:00:13.852 --> 00:00:19.699
These calculations help us understand the center, spread, and range of numerical data.

00:00:19.699 --> 00:00:26.459
For example, an analyst might calculate average daily sales, the median response time,

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:29.369
or the standard deviation of measurements.

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:37.804
Summary statistics are often the first step in exploring numerical data, but remember that one number never tells the

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:43.920
whole story. We should still inspect distributions, unusual values, and the context of the data.
